1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,200
What’s the difference between

2
00:00:01,200 --> 00:00:06,540
wa mā adrāka and wa mā yudrīka?

3
00:00:06,540 --> 00:00:09,460
In English, almost the same:

4
00:00:09,460 --> 00:00:10,900
What could make you know?

5
00:00:10,900 --> 00:00:15,340
Sufyan ibn ‘Uyaynah noted a difference:

6
00:00:15,340 --> 00:00:19,700
Wa mā adrāka: He gives an explanation.

7
00:00:19,700 --> 00:00:23,640
Wa mā yudrīka: that answer isn’t given.

8
00:00:23,640 --> 00:00:25,200
Listen to these examples.

9
00:00:25,200 --> 00:00:29,000
What can make you know

10
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:30,750
what the Night of Decree is?

11
00:00:30,750 --> 00:00:35,260
The next verse explains:

12
00:00:35,260 --> 00:00:36,600
The Night of Decree is better

13
00:00:36,600 --> 00:00:38,500
than a thousand months.

14
00:00:38,500 --> 00:00:39,700
And again:

15
00:00:39,700 --> 00:00:43,500
What can make you know

16
00:00:43,500 --> 00:00:45,000
what the night visitor is?

17
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:48,200
The piercing star.

18
00:00:48,200 --> 00:00:51,660
Both times, an explanation follows.

19
00:00:51,660 --> 00:00:53,700
Now compare wa mā yudrīka.

20
00:00:53,700 --> 00:00:59,440
What would make you know?

21
00:00:59,440 --> 00:01:01,260
Perhaps the Hour is near.

22
00:01:01,260 --> 00:01:02,600
We’re told it may be near.

23
00:01:02,600 --> 00:01:04,150
We aren’t told when.

24
00:01:04,150 --> 00:01:09,920
What would make you know?

25
00:01:09,920 --> 00:01:12,000
Perhaps he might be purified.

26
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:13,600
A possibility is mentioned.

27
00:01:13,600 --> 00:01:15,600
His outcome isn’t confirmed there.

28
00:01:15,600 --> 00:01:19,200
Next time, listen closely:

29
00:01:19,200 --> 00:01:22,540
Wa mā adrāka: an explanation follows.

30
00:01:22,540 --> 00:01:26,000
Wa mā yudrīka: the answer isn’t revealed.

31
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:29,000
They can sound similar in English…

32
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:29,800
but watch how differently

33
00:01:29,800 --> 00:01:31,820
the Qur’an uses them.
